{"type":"message","id":"c90a6989","parentId":"cf7f9bf8","timestamp":"2026-03-25T01:04:58.213Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"It seems like this is a fresh start - no memory, no identity set up yet, and the USER.md is empty. The BOOTSTRAP.md exists, which means I haven't been bootstrapped yet. Let me also check if there's a MEMORY.md and recent memory files.\n\nSince there's no memory about this user yet, and BOOTSTRAP.md exists, I should follow its guidance - start a conversation to figure out who I am and who they are. But wait, the BOOTSTRAP.md says to start with something like \"Hey. I just came online. Who am I? Who are you?\"\n\nBut actually, this appears to be coming from the \"openclaw-control-ui\" which is likely a control interface. Let me think about this more carefully.\n\nThe message is just \"hello\" - a simple greeting. Since I'm in a fresh state with no memory and no identity set up, I should probably start the bootstrap process. But the BOOTSTRAP.md says to delete it after I've figured out who I am.\n\nActually, let me just respond naturally. The user said hello. I don't have a name yet, they haven't told me who they are. I should be honest about being new and figure out who I'm talking to. Let me keep it simple and genuine.","thinkingSignature":"8da30b69d276caf8b9aaee43c4e975029cee610e85ceb31192d2c19a50da2592"},{"type":"text","text":"Hey. Looks like I'm fresh out of the box — no memory yet, no name set up. \n\nI see you've got OpenClaw running. Who are you, and what should we call me?"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":818,"output":306,"cacheRead":10468,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":11592,"cost":{"input":0.0002454,"output":0.0003672,"cacheRead":0.0006280799999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00124068}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774400686630,"responseId":"061267aff0c9dd87d29d8f2e95f65d20"}}
